// bendrt.h: runtime for C code generated by bendc (the Bend compiler written in Bend).
//
// Values are 64-bit words:
//  - numbers (U32, Char, F32 bits) are stored raw;
//  - a Nat (up to 2^48 - 1, as the official runtime's) is stored raw;
//  - nullary constructors are IMM(tag) = (tag << 3) | 1;
//  - other constructors are pointers to heap nodes {tag, fields...};
//  - closures are pointers to {fn, arity, nargs, args...}.
// A type with one constructor of one field is represented by that field.
//
// Memory is managed by a conservative, non-moving mark-sweep collector. The
// threads that run Bend code (the main thread and the fork-join workers) are
// stopped with a signal while it runs. Parallel lets fork onto a
// work-stealing pool. Effects follow the official Bend runtime's effect ABI
// (Term, Env, IoWork, io_eff, CID_*), so effect sources written for the
// official compiler (Base's own effs/*.c included) compile unchanged.

